# Topic 3 · Feminist Movements — the West, the United Nations and Pakistan

::: glance | Topic 3 at a glance
**Head IV** of the syllabus. A steady mid-weight topic: ==9.5 visits== (nine full questions and one short note, 2016–2026) and **22 of the 140 MCQs**. Two families carry it: the **waves** (2019, 2022, 2023 — an exact repeat of 2019 — 2024, 2025) and the **movement in Pakistan** (2016, 2022, 2024, 2026, plus APWA/WAF in 2018 and NGO-isation in 2026). The examiner always wants the link to Pakistan or to women's lives, and every Pakistan question carries a twist. The UN conferences have never been a full question, though MCQs on Mexico 1975, Beijing 1995 and CEDAW 1996 recur — they are due.
:::

